  "query_preview": "Forecast: Wednesday through the Weekend:\nThe remainder of the work week, beginning Wednesday, will be \ncharacterized by drier air and slightly below-normal \ntemperatures. A strong Canadian high-pressure system will spread\nsoutheast across the Midwest, keeping highs generally in the \nlow to mid 80s with no notable precipitation chances through \nThursday. A signal for warm advection-driven storms exists for \nThursday night off to our west, which may move into portions of \ncentral Illinois on Friday (20-30% chance). A warming trend will\ncommence next weekend as the surface ridge axis shifts to our \neast, allowing for a return of warmer southerly flow.",
